// Build settings for every build that ships or is checked for repeatability: the release
// archive (scripts/archive-imac.sh) and CI's repeatable job (ci/repeatable-build.sh) both pass
// this file with `-xcconfig`, so the shipped binary is built exactly as the repeatable check
// builds it. ⚠️ A file passed with -xcconfig reaches the Swift package targets; a setting in
// project.yml does not (measured: a project-level OTHER_CFLAGS left LiveKit's stubs in place).
//
// ⛔ NO OBJECTIVE-C SELECTOR STUBS. LiveKit's one Objective-C file (LKObjCHelpers.m) is
// otherwise compiled to call `objc_msgSend$<selector>` stubs, and the linker writes the
// selector references those stubs load in an order that varies between links: main's first
// run of the repeatable job (45815462034) differed in DistrictAI.app/DistrictAI that way.
// Without stubs, clang emits ordinary objc_msgSend calls and the linker has nothing to order.
OTHER_CFLAGS = $(inherited) -fno-objc-msgsend-selector-stubs
